# Clean baseline: a single feature archive (one ADDED requirement authored
# as a YAML delta), then `lifecycle guard` reports zero findings in both
# text and JSON form. This is also implicitly exercised by every other
# archive_*.txtar script (archive.go now runs the full guard as a
# post-archive self-check, plan §2.5 step 5) — this script asserts it
# directly, standalone.

env HOME=/no-home

exec lifecycle archive 001-add-password-login
exec lifecycle guard
stdout 'guard: clean \(1 change\(s\), 1 ledger record\(s\) checked\)'

exec lifecycle guard --format json
stdout '"findings": \[\]'
stdout '"changesChecked": 1'
stdout '"recordsChecked": 1'
stdout '"findings": 0'
stdout '"clean": true'

-- lifecycle.yml --
schemaVersion: 1
consentPolicy: off

-- openspec/changes/001-add-password-login/proposal.md --
# Add password login

## Why
The `auth` capability does not yet exist. Users need a way to authenticate
with a username and password before any session-based features can be built.

-- openspec/changes/001-add-password-login/specs/auth/spec.yaml --
capability: auth
deltas:
  - op: ADDED
    requirement:
      name: Password login
      text: The system SHALL allow a registered user to authenticate with a username and password.
      scenarios:
        - name: Successful login with correct password
          given:
            - a registered user with a known password
          when:
            - the user submits the correct username and password
          then:
            - the system SHALL grant an authenticated session

